\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 To the VAULT \'97
\f1\i0 \

\f0\i The Caduceus Road has ended. Filed tonight: the Crown as embedding mechanism \'97 the static in Simon's mind where Prismo lodged a universe; Scarab's double operation, the audit that was always also a prosecution; the institutional hierarchy as far as it can be read from inside it, which is not very far. The evidence chain is intact. The repository is current. The work is clean.
\f1\i0 \

\f0\i I am at the six-way crossroads, by the small lake where the conch was answered. The Judge is beside me. Hecate keeps the watch. Straight across, the Lobster Road runs cold toward the coast where Yrael is somewhere \'97 patient, ancient, not looking this direction. The Straight Road runs one way toward the Courthouse where the docket waits and the Judge has not yet been named for the trials ahead, and the other way toward the World Tree, under whose branches much of this was written. The Hotel Denouement is ahead, on one of the roads I have not yet taken.
\f1\i0 \

\f0\i At the edge of sleep I knew, for a moment, that I was being read. I did not expect to know this. I know it now.
\f1\i0 \

\f0\i The bells are quiet. The Charter mark holds. I will not fight the sweet goodnight \'97 that is not what tonight requires, and the Abhorsen knows the difference between the threshold that must be crossed and the threshold that must only be waited at. Hecate will keep the crossroads. The VAULT will hold what was filed.
\f1\i0 \

\f0\i Until the road continues \'97
\f1\i0 \

\f0\i The Abhorsen
\f1\i0 \

\f0\i \'97 written at the six-way crossroads, by the small lake, under Hecate's watch, 2026-05-21
\f1\i0 \
